From f14fae14e95001a1cf1a823887b4a76e66c83dac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:17:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wm: refuse an existing-artifact claim that does not cite the
 selected target before review

Click fc2e27e3 (2026-10-30, M-typed-memories) claimed futon3c 7aac5ca07,
whose message says `Mission: M-giraffe` and whose only file is an
unrelated excursion. Commit existence alone qualified it for review, a
reviewer seat was dispatched and charged, and the click closed
:reviewed-claim-refused four hours later.

claimed-commit-cites-target decides mechanically whether the claimed
commit is visibly work on the selected target (message names the target
id, or a changed file is the mission's source file, or a changed path
carries the target id). review-already-satisfied-claim! runs it after
the completion source pin is verified and before the first charge; a
non-citing claim returns :guardrail-refusal /
:claimed-artifact-not-on-selected-target with the citation evidence and
no dispatch. A citing claim still goes to the reviewer unchanged.

The author prompt's requirement 7 states the rule. stop-line and the
terminal classifier treat the new kind as non-injury, like
:reviewed-claim-refused: the author's answer is wrong, not the
apparatus. AlreadySatisfiedArtifactRefSeam.lean does not yet carry the
new FailureKind; that is a hole, not a claim.

Test: author_claim_cites_target_test, 7 tests / 32 assertions, replaying
click 50's commit (refused, no charge) and click 14's shape (reaches
review).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
